@page "/dev/unhandled-error"
@using Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using Backlog.UI.Components.Layout

@*
    A page whose only purpose is to break, so the app's error screen can be
    reached on purpose. The shipped app has no route that throws on request —
    and should not — which is why this lives in the harness and reaches the
    router only through the assembly App.razor hands over.

    Two ways to fail, because the boundary treats them differently. A handler
    that throws is the ordinary case: the page is fine until a click, and
    "Try again" brings it straight back. A page that throws while rendering is
    the one an error boundary has to be careful with — every attempt to draw it
    fails again — so "Try again" lands back on the error screen and "Go to Home"
    is the way out. The render failure is asked for with a query string so that
    the page can still be opened normally.
*@

<PageTitle>Unhandled error sample</PageTitle>

<div class="shell">
    <SectionHeader Title="Unhandled error sample" />

    <p>
        Development-only. Each control below throws an exception the page does not
        handle, which is what the app's error screen exists to catch.
    </p>

    <ButtonGroup>
        <AppButton TestId="sample-throw-handler" OnClick="ThrowFromHandler">Throw from a click handler</AppButton>
        <AppButton TestId="sample-throw-async" OnClick="ThrowFromAsyncHandler">Throw after an await</AppButton>
        <AppButton TestId="sample-throw-render" OnClick="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/dev/unhandled-error?render=throw"))">Throw while rendering</AppButton>
    </ButtonGroup>

    @if (Render == "throw")
    {
        throw new InvalidOperationException("The sample page threw while rendering.");
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Inject]
    private NavigationManager Navigation { get; set; } = default!;

    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "render")]
    public string? Render { get; set; }

    private static void ThrowFromHandler() =>
        throw new InvalidOperationException("The sample page threw from a click handler.");

    private static async Task ThrowFromAsyncHandler()
    {
        await Task.Yield();
        throw new InvalidOperationException("The sample page threw after an await.");
    }
}
